---
import { viewPages } from '../data/views';

const features = [
  { n: '01', title: 'Find and inspect data', body: 'Browse configured repositories, open products as file A or B, then move through groups, datasets, attributes, and statistics.' },
  { n: '02', title: 'Read data in its shape', body: 'Switch between tables, profiles, 2D slices, and 3D voxel previews. Pin dimensions and choose the axes that matter.' },
  { n: '03', title: 'See where it happened', body: 'Map satellite observations with real pixel footprints when latitude and longitude bounds are available.' },
];
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#081b2d" />
    <meta name="description" content="H5Jive is a native scientific data explorer for HDF5 and NetCDF." />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="./h5jive-icon.png" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="./site.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="./layout.css" />
    <script src="./carousel.js" defer></script>
    <script src="./releases.js" defer></script>
    <title>H5Jive — Dig into your data</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="topbar wrap">
      <a class="brand" href="#top" aria-label="H5Jive home"><img class="brand-icon" src="./h5jive.png" width="42" height="42" alt="" /> H5Jive</a>
      <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
        <a href="#capabilities">Capabilities</a>
        <a href="#views">Views</a>
        <a href="#browser">Browser</a>
        <a href="#download">Download</a>
        <a href="./plugins/">Plugins</a>
        <a href="./guide/">Guide</a>
        <a class="nav-cta" href="https://github.com/vrtulka23/h5jive">Source code <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main id="top">
      <section class="hero wrap">
        <div class="hero-top">
          <div class="hero-copy">
            <p class="eyebrow"><span class="pulse"></span> A scientific data explorer</p>
            <h1>Dig into your data.<br /><em>See the whole dataset.</em></h1>
          </div>
          <div class="hero-aside">
            <p class="lede">H5Jive turns HDF5 and NetCDF files into something you can explore: their structure, values, dimensions, and place in the world.</p>
            <div class="hero-actions">
              <a class="button primary" href="#download">Download H5Jive <span>↓</span></a>
              <a class="text-link" href="#capabilities">Explore capabilities <span>↓</span></a>
            </div>
            <div class="hero-meta"><span>BUILT WITH RUST</span><i></i><span>HDF5 · NETCDF</span><i></i><span>NATIVE DESKTOP</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="carousel" role="region" aria-label="H5Jive views" aria-roledescription="carousel">
          <div class="preview carousel-track" id="view-carousel">
            {viewPages.map((shot, i) => <figure class="carousel-slide" aria-label={`${i + 1} of ${viewPages.length}: ${shot.title}`}>
              <div class="map-art"><img src={`./${shot.image}`} width="2564" height="1508" alt={shot.alt} loading={i < 2 ? 'eager' : 'lazy'} decoding="async" /></div>
              <figcaption><span><b class="dot"></b> H5JIVE <span class="caption-divider">/</span> {shot.title.toUpperCase()}</span><a href={`./views/${shot.slug}/`}>Explore this view <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></figcaption>
            </figure>)}
          </div>
          <div class="carousel-controls">
            <button class="carousel-arrow" type="button" data-carousel-prev aria-label="Previous view">←</button>
            <div class="carousel-dots" aria-label="Choose a view">
              {viewPages.map((shot, i) => <button class="carousel-dot" type="button" data-carousel-index={i} aria-label={`Show ${shot.title.toLowerCase()} view`} aria-current={i === 0 ? 'true' : undefined}><span></span></button>)}
            </div>
            <button class="carousel-arrow" type="button" data-carousel-next aria-label="Next view">→</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="ticker" aria-label="Supported formats and views"><div class="ticker-inner">HDF5 <b>✳</b> NETCDF <b>✳</b> MULTIDIMENSIONAL ARRAYS <b>✳</b> SCAN PIXEL FOOTPRINTS <b>✳</b> HDF5 <b>✳</b> NETCDF <b>✳</b> MULTIDIMENSIONAL ARRAYS <b>✳</b> SCAN PIXEL FOOTPRINTS</div></section>

      <section id="download" class="downloads wrap">
        <div class="download-heading">
          <div><p class="eyebrow">READY TO RUN</p><h2>Download the native app.</h2></div>
          <p>Precompiled builds need no Rust toolchain. Use a portable bundle now, or choose a per-user installer when one is listed. <a href="https://github.com/vrtulka23/h5jive/releases/latest">See all release files <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
        </div>
        <p class="download-version">Latest published release: <span data-release-version>v0.1.2</span></p>
        <div class="download-grid">
          <article class="download-card">
            <span>WINDOWS / X86_64</span><h3>Windows</h3>
            <p>The setup installer installs for your user account without administrator rights. The ZIP runs from an extracted folder.</p>
            <div class="download-links">
              <a class="download-installer" data-release-asset="h5jive-windows-x86_64-setup.exe" hidden>Install for this user · .exe ↗</a>
              <a data-release-asset="h5jive-windows-x86_64.zip" href="https://github.com/vrtulka23/h5jive/releases/download/v0.1.2/h5jive-windows-x86_64.zip">Download portable ZIP ↗</a>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="download-card">
            <span>LINUX / X86_64</span><h3>Linux</h3>
            <p>The AppImage runs from your user directory without installation. The tarball contains the executable, libraries, and settings.</p>
            <div class="download-links">
              <a class="download-installer" data-release-asset="h5jive-linux-x86_64.AppImage" hidden>Download AppImage ↗</a>
              <a data-release-asset="h5jive-linux-x86_64.tar.gz" href="https://github.com/vrtulka23/h5jive/releases/download/v0.1.2/h5jive-linux-x86_64.tar.gz">Download portable tarball ↗</a>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="download-card">
            <span>MACOS / APPLE SILICON</span><h3>Mac · Apple Silicon</h3>
            <p>Open the DMG and copy H5Jive to your own Applications folder. The tarball contains the portable executable and settings.</p>
            <div class="download-links">
              <a class="download-installer" data-release-asset="h5jive-macos-aarch64.dmg" hidden>Download DMG ↗</a>
              <a data-release-asset="h5jive-macos-aarch64.tar.gz" href="https://github.com/vrtulka23/h5jive/releases/download/v0.1.2/h5jive-macos-aarch64.tar.gz">Download portable tarball ↗</a>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="download-card">
            <span>MACOS / INTEL</span><h3>Mac · Intel</h3>
            <p>Open the DMG and copy H5Jive to your own Applications folder. The tarball contains the portable executable and settings.</p>
            <div class="download-links">
              <a class="download-installer" data-release-asset="h5jive-macos-x86_64.dmg" hidden>Download DMG ↗</a>
              <a data-release-asset="h5jive-macos-x86_64.tar.gz" href="https://github.com/vrtulka23/h5jive/releases/download/v0.1.2/h5jive-macos-x86_64.tar.gz">Download portable tarball ↗</a>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
        <p class="download-note">Installer links appear when the published release includes them. All downloads are precompiled; the portable bundles need no installation.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="capabilities" class="section wrap">
        <div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">BUILT FOR EXPLORATION</p><h2>From file tree<br />to field of view.</h2><p class="section-note">Scientific data is more than a list of numbers. Keep structure, dimensions, and spatial context in view as you explore.</p></div>
        <div class="feature-list">{features.map((feature) => <article class="feature"><span class="feature-n">{feature.n}</span><div><h3>{feature.title}</h3><p>{feature.body}</p></div><span class="feature-arrow">↗</span></article>)}</div>
      </section>

      <section id="browser" class="browser-section wrap" aria-labelledby="browser-title">
        <div class="browser-heading">
          <div><p class="eyebrow">DATASET BROWSER</p><h2 id="browser-title">Find the product.<br />Then explore the data.</h2></div>
          <p>Register dataset locations in DIPL and browse their indexed products from one place. Filter sources by tag, search products by name, path, date, or orbit, and open a selection as file A or B in the inspector.</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="browser-preview">
          <img src="./dataset-browser.png" width="2564" height="1508" alt="H5Jive dataset browser showing tagged source repositories, product search, a sortable product table, and file A and B slots" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <figcaption>Configured sources on the left · searchable products on the right · selected files below</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <div class="browser-details">
          <p><strong>Keep the index close.</strong> Refresh a source when its files change; the browser saves the product list for later sessions.</p>
          <p><strong>Check a region.</strong> For geolocated products, check which files cross a selected PICS overpass area.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="./guide/settings-and-formats.html">Configure dataset sources <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="data" class="data-band">
        <div class="wrap data-content"><div><p class="eyebrow">REAL DATA, REAL FOOTPRINTS</p><h2>Scan lines you<br />can actually see.</h2><p>Explore a bundled GOME-2 Band 3 sample with 15,574 valid geolocated pixels and measured radiance across 64 spectral channels. Each pixel retains its center coordinates, four corners, and scan direction.</p><a class="button light" href="./guide/">Open the guide <span>→</span></a></div>
          <div class="data-card"><div class="card-label">IN THE EXAMPLE FILE</div><div class="data-row"><span>Instrument</span><b>GOME-2 / MetOp-B</b></div><div class="data-row"><span>Orbit</span><b>32260 · 2013-01-06</b></div><div class="data-row"><span>Variable</span><b>Band 3 radiance</b></div><div class="data-row"><span>Footprint corners</span><b>4 per pixel</b></div><div class="card-source">Source: GOME-2 Level 1B product</div></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="views" class="views wrap"><p class="eyebrow">ONE FILE, MANY ANGLES</p><div class="view-chips">{viewPages.map((view, i) => <a class="chip" href={`./views/${view.slug}/`}>{view.title}<small>0{i+1}</small></a>)}</div></section>

      <section id="plugins" class="section wrap plugin-section">
        <div class="section-intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">PLUGIN LAB</p><h2>Your science,<br />inside H5Jive.</h2></div><p class="section-note">Reuse H5Jive's HDF5 and NetCDF access, dataset selection, and visualization. Keep your analysis in its own plugin.</p></div>
        <div class="feature-list">
          <article class="feature"><span class="feature-n">01</span><div><h3>Download the source code</h3><p>Clone the open source project and try the path and value comparison demos in <code>examples/plugins/</code>.</p></div></article>
          <article class="feature"><span class="feature-n">02</span><div><h3>Implement your plugin</h3><p>You can ask an AI coding agent: “Add a Plugin Lab tool that shows the mean of my selected HDF5 dataset. Reuse H5Jive's file API and visualization views. Add a separate DIPL setting and an example.” Review and test the generated code with your data; Rust experience is not required to begin.</p></div></article>
          <article class="feature"><span class="feature-n">03</span><div><h3>Share it with scientists</h3><p>Push your plugin as a pull request to our <a href="https://github.com/vrtulka23/h5jive/tree/main/plugins">small app store</a>: the Plugin Lab catalog in the source repository. Other researchers can build on your analysis.</p></div></article>
        </div>
        <div class="plugin-actions"><a class="button primary" href="./plugins/">Explore Plugin Lab <span>→</span></a><a class="text-link" href="./guide/plugin-lab.html">Build and submit a plugin <span>→</span></a></div>
      </section>

      <section class="closing wrap"><img class="closing-icon" src="./h5jive.png" width="82" height="82" alt="" /><div><p class="eyebrow">OPEN THE PROJECT</p><h2>Start with a dataset.<br /><em>See where it leads.</em></h2></div><div class="closing-actions"><a class="button primary" href="./guide/">Read the guide <span>→</span></a><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/vrtulka23/h5jive">Browse source <span>↗</span></a></div></section>
    </main>
    <footer class="footer wrap"><a class="brand" href="#top"><img class="brand-icon" src="./h5jive.png" width="32" height="32" alt="" /> H5Jive</a><span>Dig into your data.</span><span>© H5Jive contributors</span></footer>
  </body>
</html>

